      "explanation": "First combine the fractions inside the square root using the common denominator \\(144\\):\n\\[\n\\frac19+\\frac1{16}\n=\\frac{16}{144}+\\frac9{144}\n=\\frac{25}{144}.\n\\]\nSince \\(\\left(\\frac5{12}\\right)^2=\\frac{25}{144}\\) and \\(\\frac5{12}>0\\), the principal square root is\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\frac19+\\frac1{16}}=\\boxed{\\frac5{12}},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
